It does NOT apply to the following, which remain subject to the terms of their
respective providers or to a different licence. They are included here solely so
that this application can display them, and are NOT sublicensed to you.

  data/streaming.json
      Derived from TMDB (https://www.themoviedb.org/) and JustWatch.
      Governed by the TMDB API Terms of Use
      (https://www.themoviedb.org/api-terms-of-use).
      Non-commercial use only. If you reuse this data, you must obtain your own
      TMDB API key and comply with those terms yourself.

  data/synopses.json
      Lead-section excerpts from the Japanese Wikipedia
      (https://ja.wikipedia.org/), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
      (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
      Each entry carries the article name and its URL so that the attribution
      travels with the text. If you reuse this file, you must keep that
      attribution and licence it under the same terms.

  assets/tmdb.svg
      Trademark of TMDB, included for the attribution required by their terms.
      Not licensed for any other use.

  assets/demo.gif, assets/screenshot-*.jpg
      Screenshots of the running application. The cover and banner art visible
      in them belongs to the respective rights holders.

  Note: the AniList-to-TMDB mapping used at build time comes from
  Fribb/anime-lists, derived from manami-project/anime-offline-database
  (ODbL 1.0 / DbCL 1.0). It is used for lookup only; no identifiers from it are
  written into data/streaming.json.

Content fetched at runtime is likewise owned by its providers:

  Titles, images, and schedules   AniList (https://anilist.co)
  Synopses                        Japanese Wikipedia, CC BY-SA
                                  (https://ja.wikipedia.org/)

